<title>GHANA: Ghana police clash with strikers at German firm.</title>
<headline>Ghana police clash with strikers at German firm.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five people were wounded when police in Ghana opened fire on Tuesday to break up a march by striking workers of a German construction firm, a union leader said.</p>
<p>Four of the injured were admitted to hospital in the capital Accra with gunshot wounds, union leader Dan Ofosu told reporters. The fifth was treated and released.</p>
<p>Police spokesman Musatapha Gabah said police were investigating the clash, which took place at the premises of builder Bilfinger Berger in Accra. The workers were marching to press demands for a pay increase.</p>
</text>
